            "review_title": "Review at Nephele Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Orn’s Bellyjourney\nBangkok, Thailand324 contributions\n0\nA Must-Visit for Pigeon & Poultry Lovers\nAug 2026 • Friends\nNephele was one of the restaurants I was most excited to visit during my trip to Ho Chi Minh City, and it definitely lived up to my expectations.\n\nThe restaurant focuses on modern Vietnamese cuisine, using local ingredients from different regions of Vietnam and showcasing the country’s terroir through fire-based cooking. Chef Francis Thuan has a particular talent for poultry, which has earned him the nickname “The Bird Man,” and this was especially evident in the pigeon course.\n\nThe highlight of my meal was the 3-week-old Vietnamese pigeon with mango and cacao sauce. The pigeon was unbelievably tender, with rich flavours that were beautifully balanced. It was easily one of the best pigeon dishes I’ve ever had and probably the dish I remember most from the entire meal.\n\nThe Toothfish was another favourite, and the three amuse-bouches at the beginning were also very well executed.\n\nI was also pleasantly surprised by the desserts. I’m not usually a dessert person, but both desserts were lightly sweetened and had plenty of depth. The Rice & Tea Ice Cream with warm walnut foam, caviar and fish sauce caramel was particularly memorable. It sounds like an unusual combination, but the saltiness and umami worked beautifully with the ice cream and made the flavours much more interesting.\n\nThe tasting menu also felt nicely protein-focused, with sourdough being the only bread-based course. Beyond the food, I really enjoyed the setting. The restaurant is housed in a beautiful white villa, and the bar area is equally charming, making the whole experience feel intimate and special.\n\nNephele has a strong sense of identity, both in its cooking and its setting. If you’re looking for a modern Vietnamese fine-dining experience in Ho Chi Minh City, this is definitely a restaurant I would recommend.\nRead more\nWritten August 19, 2026",
