            "review_text": "jwie86\nOslo, Norway50 contributions\n0\nA Tasting Menu with Character\nDec 2025 • Friends\nThis is quite the memorable restaurant I went to in Vietnam. It's a wonderful journey that hits you in all your senses and has character/heart. \n\nYou start your journey in Nephele going into the living room (the downstairs area) and actually start your tasting menu journey here. This doubles as a bar and has a modern/cozy look. We were served drinks and some of our first amuse bouches here which were delicious. \n\nSomething I wanted to add here is that I have some current medical conditions that prevent me from eating raw food. The kitchen was so kind in their substitutions and from all the substitutions I had, these were some of the best. \n\nAfter eating our first bites, we were taken up to the kitchen which had a really unique look - paper machete ceilings and walls. We were given a table that could easily see the kitchen at work. The owner, Paul, was super kind to us and my fiancee's dad - speaking to us both in English and Vietnamese. And he was quite a character - telling stories about the ingredients, the chef, and his own life that infused so much life into the entire experience. The party got to even drink a special holiday chilled sweet wine that he had. \n\nSome more of the favorite bites from the 12ish menu items included:\n*the shriako - was the replacement for the uni in the opener and was so delightful. All three bites in this set were incredible.\n*the sourdough - so wonderful. The sourdough itself was well baked and the truffle butter, honeycomb, and miso butter were such wonderful complements and unique. One of our friends asked for another slice as that was offered, and the kitchen actually brought out a whole loaf for him.\n*caviar, roasted ice cream, fish sauce walnut: a wonderful dessert concept. The caviar and fish sauce didn't overpower the ice cream at all. Instead, it reminded me of a wonderful version of sea salt ice cream and think it came out so memorable. \n\nAfter our last main dessert, we were taken back down to the living room to chill as the room became a casual bar with vinyls playing holiday music. The chef himself came down, Francis Thuan, and chatted with us along with the owner. We got to both give our favorite dishes and overall feedback. \n\nOverall, just a wonderful and hospitable experience that I won't forget. Would totally come back for another round to see how the cooking has evolved!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 16, 2026",
